## Report
Validated the availability finding with targeted Rust unit PoCs plus an LLDB trace. Direct crash attempt: `cargo test -p storage --lib poc_ -- --nocapture` did not crash, which is expected for this logical availability bug, but both PoC tests passed. Valgrind was unavailable (`valgrind: command not found`), and ASan could not be used on the stable toolchain (`-Z sanitizer=address` rejected as nightly-only). Debugger attempt succeeded with LLDB: a breakpoint at `crates/storage/src/cluster.rs:1337` showed the installer thread in `StorageClusterRouteAdmissionGate::begin_publication`, called from `StorageClusterRuntimeMapHandle::install` at `cluster.rs:1621`, matching the suspected blocking publication path.

Code evidence: `acquire()` waits while the gate is not Open and increments `active_requests` at `crates/storage/src/cluster.rs:1302-1321`; `begin_publication()` sets Draining and waits for `active_requests == 0` at `cluster.rs:1324-1347`; the request permit is only released on `Drop` at `cluster.rs:1388-1399`; `install()` only checks that candidate validity is bounded before `begin_publication()` and does not revalidate after draining at `cluster.rs:1610-1621`. Streaming PUT acquires admission after auth at `crates/server-http/src/http/mod.rs:4142-4145`, stores it in `StreamingPutContext` at `mod.rs:4274-4277` and in the struct at `mod.rs:4777-4783`; the async body loop keeps `Arc<ctx>` alive while repeatedly waiting on `tokio::time::timeout(idle_timeout, body.frame())` at `crates/server-http/src/http/serve.rs:3112-3125`, so a slow body can retain the permit across per-frame waits.

Dynamic evidence: added `poc_held_frontend_route_stalls_publication_and_later_admissions`, which holds an admitted route, starts `install()`, waits until publication is pending, starts a later admission, sleeps 100ms, and asserts both `installed_rx.try_recv()` and `admitted_rx.try_recv()` are still empty until the original admission is dropped. Added `poc_expired_candidate_can_be_published_after_drain`, which starts publication with a candidate valid until 1500ms, advances test time to 2000ms before releasing the held admission, and proves `install()` publishes that candidate by asserting `handle.current()` is the candidate and `require_route_map_valid_now()` returns `RouteMapExpired { valid_until_ms: 1500, now_ms: 2000 }`. Test output: `running 2 tests ... ok ... test result: ok. 2 passed; 0 failed`.

